-- term.lth: the kernel term as data, and the theories of its names, substitution, canonical form
-- and reduction.
--
-- Draft 0, 2026-10-13, by Claude Opus 5.5 in the session (step 2.2 of
-- record/plan-from-zero-2026-10-13-execution.md). Sources: spec 3 §4 (3.S14 to 3.S20, the five
-- rules of reduction), §6 (3.S29 to 3.S35, programs as data), 3.S38 (this file), 3.S11 (fuel);
-- L2.7 (each constructor has a law of its role); D-2026-10-12-x, D-2026-10-12-ah. The pattern is
-- that of ebnf.lth: a theory is a record type of its operations, laws over a model, `T := laws`;
-- its model is a value in a `.lut`. Here the main model is `reduce`, the interpreter written in
-- Luthier (3.S33), in term_model.lut; the host's evaluator is a second specimen of the same theory
-- (L14.3), as `backtrack` and the Python recognizer are of `Derives`.
--
-- On meaning (L2.7). The constructors of `Term` that compute get their roles from the laws of
-- `Reduction` (§5): `Lam` and `App` from `Beta`, `Var` from `Delta`, `Match`, `Inj` and `Pair`
-- from `Iota`, `Lit` from `Prim`, `Extern` from `ExternCall`, `Hole` from `HolesStay`. The type
-- formers (`Universe`, `World`, `Pi`, `Sigma`, `Sum`, `Data`, `Subtype`) are values for reduction
-- (`ValuesStay`); their roles are the checker's, laws of `WellFormed` in program.lth (step 3.1).
--
-- Names: the constructors are 3.S29's, capitalized as there, so that they do not clash with the
-- surface tree of grammar.lth when the translation of 2.S12 imports both; `U` is a keyword, so the
-- universe is `Universe`; `World` is added for `W` (D-2026-10-13-b), which 3.S29 predates.
--
-- Index. Status of each section: done, or todo with what it needs. A session or Codex continuing
-- this file takes the first todo, writes it in the pattern of the done ones and of kernel_laws.lth,
-- checks it with `luthier parse src/luthier/lib/term.lth`, sets its status to done here, commits.
--
--   §1 The data: `Literal`, `Term`, `Pattern`, `Act`, `Program` (3.S29, 3.S30, 3.S31).     todo
--   §2 Names: free variables, renaming, alpha-equivalence as an object with the
--      law of renaming a bound variable (3.S31, L3.3; `Object` of kernel_laws.lth).     todo
